From: AmberELEC battery longevity
Subject: [PATCH] rk3326-rg351mp: gentler battery charge/discharge thresholds

Reduce wear on the single-cell LiPo:
- Power-off / discharge cutoff 3000 -> 3400 mV to keep a reserve and avoid
  deep discharge (also aligns with the capacity 0% point in the fuel gauge).

Applied to both the default and the timing_fix device tree of the RG351MP.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-rg351mp-linux.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-rg351mp-linux.dts
@@ -1255,7 +1255,7 @@
 			sleep_enter_current = <300>;
 			sleep_exit_current = <300>;
 			sleep_filter_current = <100>;
-			power_off_thresd = <3000>;
+			power_off_thresd = <3400>;
 			zero_algorithm_vol = <3850>;
 			max_soc_offset = <60>;
 			monitor_sec = <5>;
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-rg351mp-linux-timing_fix.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3326-rg351mp-linux-timing_fix.dts
@@ -1255,7 +1255,7 @@
 			sleep_enter_current = <300>;
 			sleep_exit_current = <300>;
 			sleep_filter_current = <100>;
-			power_off_thresd = <3000>;
+			power_off_thresd = <3400>;
 			zero_algorithm_vol = <3850>;
 			max_soc_offset = <60>;
 			monitor_sec = <5>;
